Customer benefit
The new feature:
• Helps reduce the risk of duplicate processing
• Creates a smoother and more reliable payment experience
What Mastercard is doing
Mastercard is introducing an Authorization Request Duplicate Protection
capability on the Mastercard Network that detects and declines
duplicate authorization requests for MoneySend Payment Transactions
and Gaming Payment Transactions based on certain criteria.
This capability verifies for MoneySend Payment and Gaming Payment
Transaction Request/0100 messages and Financial Transaction Request/
0200 messages switched on the Mastercard Network (the "New
Message") whether or not they meet the following conditions in relation
to previously effected authorization request message (the "Original
Message")
1. Both the Original Message and the New Message were
authorization requests for MoneySend Payment or a Gaming
Payment Transaction.
2. Both the Original Message and the New Message were switched
over the Mastercard Network.
