Message flows
Mastercard will detect duplications of MoneySend Payment and Gaming Payment Authorization Request/0100
and Financial Transaction Request/0200 messages. The detection criteria will include:
• DE 2 (Primary Account Number [PAN])
• DE 7 (Transmission Date and Time) - up to minutes will be considered
• DE 11 (Systems Trace Audit Number [STAN])
• DE 32 (Acquiring Institution ID Code)
• DE 33 (Forwarding Institution ID Code), when present
• DE 42 (Acceptor ID), when present
Mastercard will automatically decline duplicate requests by generating an Authorization Request Response/
0110 or Financial Transaction Request Response/0210 message containing:
• DE 39 (Response Code), existing value 94 (Duplicate transmission detected)
• DE 48 (Additional Data: Private Use), subelement 84 (Merchant Advice Code) new value as described in the
data element tables in this release announcement
Testing
Mastercard recommends testing to support the enhancements described in this release announcement.
